      "title": "Part-Time Simulation Technician, Clinical Learning Center",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\n\nLocation: Rockville Centre\n\nAPPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS: Interested applicants should submit the following materials with their application: Cover Letter  Resume TYPE OF POSITION/EMPLOYMENT CATEGORY: Part-Time DEPARTMENT: Clinical learning Center SCHEDULE: Hours may range from 7am to 10pm, Monday through Friday Occasional evening, weekend, and holiday hours may be required to support simulation activities and University events. REMOTE WORK:   No HOURS/WEEK and MONTHS/YEAR: 21 hours/week and 44 weeks (10-Month position) FLSA STATUS: Non-Exempt (Hourly) GENERAL PURPOSE Operate, maintain, and troubleshoot simulation equipment, task trainers, audiovisual systems, and simulation software to support simulation-based learning activities. Assist faculty, staff, and students with the preparation, execution, and evaluation of simulation experiences. Program and manage simulation scenarios, maintain equipment readiness, and support the effective operation of the Clinical Learning Center. Demonstrate flexibility in scheduling and responsibilities to meet departmental and University needs. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES   Set up supplies, equipment, and simulation environments to meet learning objectives and rapidly prepare rooms for subsequent simulation events. Clean, maintain, and prepare simulators and task trainers, including removal of adhesives and moulage, flushing IV systems, and performing routine equipment care. Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues across Clinical Learning Center facilities, ensuring simulators, task trainers, and equipment are properly stored and maintained. Maintain simulation supplies and equipment inventory, assist with equipment maintenance and repairs, support daily Clinical Learning Center operations, and assist with faculty communications, including distributing simulation schedules, updates, and instructional information. REQUIRED MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS  Bachelor's Degree 5-8 years of work related experience Microsoft Office (Excel, Outlook, Word) PREFFERED MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Microsoft PowerPoint RESPONSIBILITY FOR PUBLIC CONTACT Daily contact requiring courtesy, discretion, and sound judgment. SALARY INFORMATION When determining the salary offer for a new employee, Molloy considers several key characteristics such as job knowledge, skills, and experience as well as internal and external equity. The hiring hourly rate for this position is $27.93 to $34.90 This hourly rate represents the University's good faith and reasonable estimate of the range of compensation at the time of posting.   As part of its total compensation package, Molloy University offers an extensive range of  benefits and programs  for its employees including generous time off and tuition benefits. For further information, please visit  Benefits | Molloy University .  AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER  Women, minorities, persons with disabilities and veterans are encouraged to apply.  Molloy University does not discriminate on the basis of an individual's race, color, national origin, religion, creed, age, disability, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, familial status, pregnancy, predisposing genetic characteristics, or military status; in its administration of educational policies, programs or activities; its admissions policies; or in employment practices.   Molloy University takes its responsibility seriously to establish an environment in which the dignity and worth of all members of the institutional community are respected. In its effort to provide an optimal learning environment the University seeks the appointment of persons who are highly qualified and whose background is appropriate to fill each vacancy. It is University policy to recruit, employ, retain and promote employees without discrimination regarding sex, race, color, creed, religion, age, marital status, sexual orientation, veteran status, national or ethnic origin or physical disability.",
